Z||000037||Mach10||12-21-2001||06:53 PM||||"My daddy is a heart-surgeon, so I'm the most qualified doctor here!" Sorry, was THAT what you are saying, Johnny?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>Hmm... unstable hydrocarbons in a non-hermetically sealed container... Those'll last long. <P>Some bullets misfire after a year<BR>Some bullets do not misfire after a year<BR>THEREFORE All bullets do not misfire after a year.<P>Nice logic!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000038||ejayerik||12-21-2001||07:05 PM||||You know, I own a Beretta M92 (9MM) in which I lost one of my three clips fully loaded. (Don't ask) Anywho, about a year and a half later I found it in an old lockbox in the garage. I dusted it off, reloaded it with the same ammo, and took it down to the range where I fired the ammo. It fired just fine. No misfires, no swollen bullets, and none of them got stuck in the chamber. I'd say give it awhile before giving up the ammo.||||reg||1
Z||000039||reddog||12-21-2001||09:33 PM||||Why do I even bother trying.What the hell is wrong with everyone these days? Seems like all some of you guys want to do is chime in and argue. I offered my opinion because the man asked a question. Some little *******  wants to cut in and call everyone names and start problems. My statements were not just my opinion they are the opinion of every certified Law Enforcement Officer in the U.S.A. Did I call myself an expert? No, but maybe I should have.<BR>Here are some of my qualifications.<BR>4 years Army infantry (Ranger qualified)<BR>5 Years Law Enforcement. (Patrolman/Training)<BR>Certified NRA Police Firearms Instructor<BR>Certified NRA Security Firearms Instructor<BR>Certified Armed Security Firearms Instructor through the Tennessee Dept. of Commerce and Insurance.<BR>Certified Glock transition Firearms Instructor through Glock Inc.<BR>Certified Glock Armorer<BR>Attended the NRA Law Enforcement Firearms Instructor Development School at the FBI Training Academy in Quantico, Va.<BR>Member Of IALEFI / International Association of Law Enforcement Firearms Instructors<BR>Member of ASLET / American Society of Law Enforcement Trainers<BR>Attended training conferences every year with both organizations.<BR>My statement reflected what is taught by every single legitimate Firearms Instructor in the country. Not just an opinion. But I guess there is always some jackass out there who would argue even if God himself told them they were wrong. Thanks to Theogre and artherd for trying to help these guys out. But I am afraid that it is pointless.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000040||BN Boomer||12-22-2001||10:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Yup.. the ol "my buddies defense"... So, my friend went hunting a few months ago, and was out of 6mm x 55, so i gave him some that were sitting there for god knows how long (a lot longer than me, probably), and wouldn't you know it, no misfires..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So, was there any danger of whatever he was hunting attacking him or shooting back? If not, then no big deal. I ,ay use the same box of 30-06 to hunt deer and elk with for several years myself. But if so, do what you want, but I value my own life consideraly more than a box of new catridges.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Anyways, I am also out of this conversation.<BR>It is not my place to divulge who owns what if they don't want me to..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Translation: I don't own any guns so I don't even meet my own criteria to be dispensing advice about this subject.||||reg||1
Z||000041||JohnnyK||12-22-2001||07:02 PM||||Mach: Stop trying to argue with me in every thread just for the sake of arguing with me. So if my father is a dental surgeon, than I must not know any more than the average guy about dental surgery? Yeeeah.....?  Anyways, ammunition is perfectly sealed if correct, nothing getting in or out (hence the theory why it works)..||||reg||1
Z||000042||BN Boomer||12-22-2001||07:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Anyways, ammunition is perfectly sealed if correct, nothing getting in or out (hence the theory why it works)..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, most commercially produced ammunition IS NOT "perfectly sealed". And even if it were "perfectly sealed", how would that protect the gunpowder and primer from the degrading effects of heat and temperature fluctuations? <P>You know, the web is full of websites dealing with firearms related issues. Why don't you try doing little research before posting such nonsense? <P>If this is the kind of information you get from your dad, for the sake of his patients I hope he is a far more competent dentist than he is gun owner/collector.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000043||REDHOTT88||12-22-2001||07:35 PM||||With your apparent wealth of knowledge in firearms, that you love to spew out, why don't you start your own website. <P>I thought the people on this forum were all Fiero owners who shared a common bond... <P>Maybe not everyone on the forum has your self proclaimed, collossal expertise in firearms, but trying to cut down everybody who says something because you believe you are just so far superior, isn't the way to win respect with the forum members..     <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/fury.gif">    <P>When someone posts an answer to a technical question, I don't see any body rattling off all they're credentials to justify their answer.. Nor do I see anyone cutting down the previous response.<P>You guys need to relax just a bit... stop trying to impress everyone with your "I'm better than you, because I know something you don't" responses!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/tosser1.gif">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000044||BN Boomer||12-22-2001||07:55 PM||||REDHOTT, despite your own personal interpretation, I'm not trying to impress anyone. What I am doing is providing informed, correct information to a question regarding a subject in which I do have extensive experience and knowledge. <P>If you don't like that someone has more knowledge about a given subject than you or anyone else, tough tiddley-winks. Either become more informed about it yourself, stay on the sidelines, or if you must post inaccuracies, at least be prepared to have someone point them out and accept it. <P>If you have something of note to contribute to this discussion then by all means feel free to do so. Otherwise, simply ignore the thread if it bothers you so much. Is that really too much to ask?<P>If I came in here posting that my 85 Fiero GT came stock with 300hp and I beat Ferraris every night, could I reasonably not expect someone to either ask for clarification or question the legitimacy of my claim?||||reg||1
Z||000045||BN Boomer||12-22-2001||08:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>With your apparent wealth of knowledge in firearms, that you love to spew out, why don't you start your own website. <P>Maybe not everyone on the forum has your self proclaimed, collossal expertise in firearms, <I>but trying to cut down everybody who...</I></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I also just thought I'd point out the irony of someone who, in the process of complaining about a fellow forum member supposedly cutting down others, somehow manages sarcasm and put downs of his own.<P>Have a nice day and Merry Christmas! [ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">]||||reg||1
Z||000046||REDHOTT88||12-22-2001||08:07 PM|||| I gotcha.. BUT, if you read thru this thread, it really sounds like everyone is trying to out answer the next guy, and show off their gun collection. <P>Maybe I took some of it the wrong way, (probably due to all the coffee I drank..) but the original post just asked a simple question, and everybody jumped in and gave him info as if he was a child.. <P>Notice he hasn't posted since?<P>Anyways, I guess I'll stay away from this topic.<P>I love guns, have more than I need, but not as many as I want.. and I shoot often.<BR> <BR>God Bless America and have a Merry Christmas!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000047||BN Boomer||12-22-2001||08:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B>if you read thru this thread, it really sounds like everyone is trying to out answer the next guy... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, when I go back and reread the thread, I think most people were trying to provide helpful answers. Maybe the ogre was a little abrasive, but that's just his style. Direct and to the point. It wasn't until someone else came in and started posting erroneous information along with challenging what is recognized by every leading authority on the subject of firearms and some of us felt compelled to correct him that things started spinning a bit out of control.<P>You'll also note that in my very first reply I actually generally agree with what Johnny has been saying. Old ammunition usually does work okay. The problem is that when one's safety and well-being are on the line, "usually" just isn't good enough. You want to minimize every chance for Murphy to impose his law. This means keeping fresh, reliable amminition in firearms that you may have to call upon to defend your very life. <P>You know what? I'm kind of tired of beating this horse, too. Maybe Johnny just isn't concerned about the defensive use or applications of firearms. Are Canadians allowed to carry concealed weapons?||||reg||1
Z||000048||REDHOTT88||12-22-2001||08:36 PM||||OK, I'll bury the hatchet with you.. (nods head, reaches out to shake hands..) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>My rant wasn't just concerning your posts.<P> But you're right, this horse is quite dead... (do you smell something funny?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
