Z||000050||Mach10||12-23-2001||12:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Mach: Stop trying to argue with me in every thread just for the sake of arguing with me. So if my father is a dental surgeon, than I must not know any more than the average guy about dental surgery? Yeeeah.....?  Anyways, ammunition is perfectly sealed if correct, nothing getting in or out (hence the theory why it works)..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>If only we had a bigger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> smilie  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>FYI: I haven't even POSTED to any of your responses since Sept... Where do you get this stuff?<P>Yep. Just because your dad is a dental surgeon, doesn't mean that you know anything more about dental surgery. Unless, of course, that you truly beleive that you can learn by osmosis, or that your father has been training you on the subject. Same thing goes for your "Friend." If he knows something, show him in.<P>And ammo is NOT perfectly sealed. It lets moisture and other stuff in, just fine.||||reg||1
